{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>He shall not multiply horses for himself.</b> But only enough for his chariot — so that he does not <b>cause the people to return to Egypt</b>, for horses come from there, as is said of Solomon (I Kings 10): ״וַתַּעֲלֶה וַתֵּצֵא מֶרְכָּבָה מִמִּצְרַיִם בְּשֵׁשׁ מֵאוֹת כֶּסֶף וְסוּס בַּחֲמִשִּׁים וּמֵאָה״ (Sanhedrin 21)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:28.124200609Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}